{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>So Jeshurun grew fat and kicked.</b> Behold, even among them the masters of inquiry who are called Jeshurun, from אֲשׁוּרֶנּוּ (Numbers 24:17), acted like beasts that kick at the people who feed them." "<b>You grew fat, you grew thick, you became gross.</b> You, O Jeshurun — the assembly of those who grasp the Torah and are masters of inquiry — turned toward physical pleasures, and thereby you grew thick from apprehending the subtlety of truth, as it says: וְגַם אֵלֶּה בַּיַּיִן שָׁגוּ וּבַשֵּׁכָר תָּעוּ כֹּהֵן וְנָבִיא (Isaiah 28:7)." "<b>You became gross.</b> As it says (Isaiah 44:18): כִּי טַח מֵרְאוֹת עֵינֵיהֶם מֵהַשְׂכִּיל לִבּוֹתָם." "<b>And he forsook Eloah who made him.</b> And consequently the multitude forsook Eloah who made him." "<b>And he spurned the Rock of his salvation.</b> He held Him in contempt, for from evil to evil they went forth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:02.930574946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}